window.docContents[212].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Synopsis--Verifiable-properties":{"contents":"* assemble of the two bodies' masses gives the pair's mass as an IndividualQuantity about the pair as a whole (type-checked) HCP.L2_ThePair#pair_mass.* Adding the pair's mass to body A's mass fails with a type mismatch, because one is about the whole and the other about a part; adding pair P's mass to pair Q's mass fails the same way (refused) HCP.L2_ThePair#refused_whole_part.* assemble of angular frequency over the pair's bodies fails to type-check: there is no Assembles pairS instance for angular frequency (refused) HCP.L2_ThePair#refused_frequency_assembly.* The normal-mode frequency ω₊ is an angular-frequency kind dedicated to the sort pairS, and it is provably different from any angular-frequency kind dedicated to a body or a spring (type-checked) HCP.L2_ThePair#normal_mode.* assemble of stiffness over springs in parallel type-checks; over springs in series it fails: there is no Assembles seriesS springConstantK instance (refused) HCP.L2_ThePair#parallel_stiffness, HCP.L2_ThePair#refused_series_stiffness.* The parallel assembly equals the measured stiffness of the parallel combination, and the series law 1/k = 1/k₁ + 1/k₂ gives k = 2 for springs of stiffness 6 and 3 (theorem) HCP.L2_ThePair#parallelLaw, HCP.L2_ThePair#licenseCashed, HCP.L2_ThePair#seriesLaw.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L2 — The pair is a system too\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.3.1.3. Verifiable properties","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Synopsis--Verifiable-properties"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--The-Proved-Spine--Examination-___-principle___-method___-procedure-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-7___-14_RPAR_":{"contents":"\n\nThe examination chain has three layers — an examination principle (§7.5 / VIM4\n2CD 2.4), a method based on a principle (VIM4 2CD 2.5), and a procedure based\non a method (VIM4 2CD 2.7) — gathered into one carrier ExaminationItem so that refinement\nis a homogeneous relation. The forgetful projection basePrinciple sends any\nitem down to the principle it rests on.\n\nThree small structures with DecidableEq, united by an ExaminationItem\ninductive; basePrinciple is the projection to the principle layer.\n\nAn examination method (Dybkær Ch. 7 / VIM4 2CD 2.5) is a generic description of\nan examination, based on an examination principle.\n\nA structure carrying an identifier and the ExaminationPrinciple it is based on.\n\nAn examination procedure (Dybkær Ch. 7 / VIM4 2CD 2.7) is a detailed description,\nbased on an examination method; its principle is\nthe method's principle.\n\nA structure carrying an identifier and the ExaminationMethod it is based on.\n\nRefinement Refines is the reflexive–transitive closure of the \"based-on\"\nedges (a procedure is based on its method, a method on its principle): procedure\n⊑ method ⊑ principle. It mirrors specialization over\nkinds — the same closure construction, one level down at the defining aspect.\n\nAn inductive with refl and step constructors over a BasedOn edge\nrelation; of_basedOn lifts a single edge.\n\nRefinement is a preorder. It is reflexive (the refl constructor) and\ntransitive (Refines.trans) on the examination chain — the\nsame algebraic law proved for specialization, which an OWL2 reasoner can neither\nstate nor prove.\n\nTransitivity is by induction on the first derivation, exactly as for\nSpecializes: refl returns the second derivation, step re-applies the\nconstructor under the inductive hypothesis.\n\nRefinement preserves the principle. Every examination in one refinement chain\nrests on the same base principle:\n\nThe forgetful projection to the principle layer is invariant along refinement —\nthe examination-layer analogue of  being a homomorphism, and one provable\nhere in the Mathlib-free core without PhysLib. Builds on refinement.\n\nBy induction on the refinement derivation: each BasedOn edge preserves the base\nprinciple (cases … <;> rfl), and the inductive step chains the resulting\nequalities.\n\nThe examination principle is a defining aspect. Two kinds\nexamined by different principles are distinct kinds — independently of scale and\ndimension. This is what keeps width and height distinct while both remain\nrational lengths, mutually comparable under their\nshared super-kind Length.\n\nThe kinds differ in their examPrinciple field, so they are unequal by\ncongruence: substitute the assumed kind-equality and derive a contradiction from\nthe field inequality.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009The Proved Spine","header":"6.4. Examination — principle, method, procedure (Dybkær Ch. 7, 14)","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--The-Proved-Spine--Examination-___-principle___-method___-procedure-_LPAR_Dybk___r-Ch___-7___-14_RPAR_"}});